U('null-result',1,'空结果与操作失败','API 文档',[
 ['The FindItem method searches the current collection for an item with the specified identifier. If a matching item exists, the method returns that item. If the search completes successfully but no match is found, it returns null. A null result therefore does not mean that the operation failed. It means that the requested item is absent from the collection at the time of the search.','FindItem 方法在当前集合中查找具有指定标识符的项目。如果存在匹配项，就返回该项。如果查找成功完成但没有匹配项，则返回 null。因此，null 结果并不表示操作失败，而是表示查找时集合中不存在所请求的项目。'],
 ['Invalid input is handled differently. Passing an empty identifier causes the method to throw an argument exception. Callers should validate user input before performing a search and should still handle the no-match case after the call. Do not assume that validation guarantees a result: a valid identifier may refer to an item that was removed by another operation. The method does not create a new item when a search returns null.','无效输入的处理方式不同。传入空标识符会导致方法抛出参数异常。调用方应在查找前验证用户输入，调用后仍应处理未找到的情况。不要以为验证通过就保证有结果：有效的标识符可能指向已被其他操作删除的项目。查找返回 null 时，该方法不会创建新项目。'],
 ['For example, a settings page might display a short message saying that the item is no longer available, while keeping the rest of the page usable. This is usually more helpful than showing a general error dialog. Log unexpected exceptions separately from ordinary no-match results so that routine user actions do not fill the error log. If the application needs to create a missing item, use a separate operation and make that behaviour clear to the user.','例如，设置页面可以显示一条简短消息，说明项目已不可用，同时保持页面其余部分可用。这通常比显示通用错误弹窗更有帮助。将意外异常与普通未匹配结果分开记录，以免日常用户操作塞满错误日志。如果应用需要创建缺失项目，请使用单独操作，并向用户说明该行为。']
],[['specified identifier','指定的标识符','Search for the specified identifier.'],['no match is found','未找到匹配项','Return null if no match is found.'],['handle the case','处理这种情况','Handle the no-match case.'],['do not assume','不要假定','Do not assume that a valid ID exists.'],['separately from','与……分开','Log exceptions separately from empty results.']],[[
 'null 在这段文档中表示什么？',['查找完成但没有匹配项','必然发生异常','系统自动创建了新项'],0,'第一段明确区分成功查找但无匹配与操作失败。'],
 ['输入验证通过后，为什么仍需处理 null？',['验证会清空集合','对应项目仍可能已经被移除','null 只能表示空字符串'],1,'有效的标识符不保证对应项仍存在。'],
 ['文中建议如何记录普通未匹配结果？',['全部记录为意外异常','阻止用户再搜索','与意外异常区分处理'],2,'最后一段建议分开记录，避免把普通操作都当作错误。']
 ],{task:'为一个查找方法写一段英文说明，区分“未找到”和“调用失败”。',audience:'使用该方法的开发者',length:'90～140 词',requirements:['解释正常返回值与未找到的结果','说明无效输入的处理方式','提醒调用方处理找不到的情况，不承诺自动创建'],starter:'This method searches…\nA null result means…',model:'This method searches the collection for an item with the given identifier. It returns the matching item when one exists, or null when the search finishes without a match. A null result is an expected outcome, not an exception. An empty identifier is invalid and causes an argument exception. Validate user input before calling the method, but still check the result afterwards. Another operation may have removed the item even if its identifier is valid. The method does not create missing items. If creation is required, perform it through a separate operation.'});
U('bug-report',1,'可复现的问题报告','Issue',[
 ['The application closes unexpectedly when I remove a tab after opening the settings panel. I can reproduce the problem in a new project, so it does not appear to depend on my existing project data. The problem occurs on version 2.4 of the training application. I have not tested earlier versions, and I do not yet know whether the same behaviour occurs on other operating systems.','在打开设置面板后移除标签页时，应用会意外关闭。我能在新项目中复现，因此问题似乎不依赖现有项目数据。问题发生在此练习应用的 2.4 版。我尚未测试更早版本，也不知道其他操作系统上是否同样发生。'],
 ['To reproduce it, create a new project and open two tabs. Open the settings panel, leave the default options unchanged, and then close the panel. Finally, remove the second tab. I expect the remaining tab to stay open and the application to continue running. Instead, the entire application closes. Closing a tab before opening the settings panel does not produce the same result in my tests.','复现步骤：创建新项目并打开两个标签页。打开设置面板，保留默认选项，再关闭该面板。最后移除第二个标签页。预期是剩余标签页保持打开，应用继续运行；实际却是整个应用关闭。在我的测试中，如果尚未打开设置面板就关闭标签页，不会出现同样结果。'],
 ['I have attached the log from the failed session and a short recording of these steps. The recording contains only sample data. I have not identified the cause, so I am reporting the sequence of actions rather than claiming that a particular component is responsible. If more information would help, please tell me which environment details or logs you need. I can also test a proposed fix against the same steps.','我已附上失败会话的日志及简短操作录屏，录屏只包含示例数据。由于尚未找到原因，我报告的是操作顺序，而不是声称某个组件一定有问题。若需要更多信息，请说明需要哪些环境信息或日志。我也可以按相同步骤测试修复方案。']
],[['reproduce the problem','复现问题','I can reproduce the problem.'],['default options','默认选项','Keep the default options unchanged.'],['expected behaviour','预期行为','Describe the expected behaviour.'],['rather than','而不是','Report observations rather than guesses.'],['proposed fix','提出的修复方案','I can test the proposed fix.']],[[
 '作者是否确认是设置面板组件导致崩溃？',['已经确认','没有，只报告观察到的操作顺序','确认是操作系统问题'],1,'最后一段明确说明尚未识别原因，不把观察当作因果结论。'],
 ['哪一步顺序是报告中的关键条件？',['先关闭应用，再打开标签','必须修改所有默认选项','先开关设置面板，再移除第二个标签'],2,'报告指出在未打开设置面板前关闭标签不会复现同样结果。'],
 ['作者希望移除标签后发生什么？',['剩余标签保持打开，应用继续运行','所有标签都关闭','项目被删除'],0,'第二段明确写出了 expected behaviour。']
 ],{task:'用英文报告一个你遇到过的软件问题；没有真实问题时，可以使用文中的场景。',audience:'项目维护者',length:'100～160 词',requirements:['给出环境和可复现步骤','分开写预期与实际结果','区分已观察的事实和尚未确认的原因'],starter:'Steps to reproduce:\nExpected behaviour:\nActual behaviour:',model:'The app closes when I remove a tab after opening the settings panel. I reproduced this in a new project on version 2.4. First, create a project and open two tabs. Next, open and close the settings panel without changing any options. Then remove the second tab. I expect the first tab to remain open, but the entire app closes instead. Removing a tab before opening settings does not cause the same problem in my tests. I have attached a log containing sample data. I have not confirmed the cause and can provide more environment details if needed. I can also test a suggested workaround and report the result.'});
U('clarify',1,'把模糊需求问清楚','书面协作',[
 ['Thanks for the request to make the dashboard update in real time. Before I start, I would like to clarify what “real time” means for this screen. Do users need to see every individual event, or is a summary refreshed every few seconds sufficient? These two requirements would lead to different designs, especially when the connection is slow or temporarily unavailable.','谢谢你提出让仪表盘实时更新的需求。开始之前，我想澄清这个页面上的“实时”具体是什么意思：用户需要看到每个独立事件，还是每隔几秒更新一次摘要就足够？这两种要求会导致不同设计，尤其在网络缓慢或暂时不可用时。'],
 ['I also need to know how the screen should behave when fresh data cannot be loaded. One option is to keep showing the most recent values with a visible timestamp. Another is to replace the values with an unavailable state. Keeping old values may help users continue their work, but it could be misleading if they assume the values are current. We should choose a behaviour based on the decisions people make from this screen.','我还需要知道无法加载新数据时页面应如何表现。一种方案是继续展示最近的值并显示时间戳，另一种是改为不可用状态。保留旧值可能帮助用户继续工作，但如果用户以为这些值仍是当前值，就会产生误导。应根据用户如何利用页面作决策来选择。'],
 ['Could you confirm the acceptable delay, the expected number of active users, and the preferred fallback behaviour? A short example of a typical user task would be useful too. Once these points are clear, I can propose an implementation and estimate the work. For now, I have written down the assumptions rather than treating them as approved requirements. Please correct anything that does not match your intention.','能否确认可接受的延迟、预计活跃用户数量，以及偏好的降级行为？如果能给一个典型用户任务的简短例子，也会很有用。这些点明确后，我可以提出实现方案并估算工作量。目前我只是记录了假设，没有将它们视为已批准的需求。若有任何与原意不符的地方，请纠正。']
],[['clarify','澄清','I would like to clarify the requirement.'],['sufficient','足够的','A short summary may be sufficient.'],['most recent','最近的','Show the most recent values.'],['fallback behaviour','降级或备用行为','Confirm the fallback behaviour.'],['assumption','假设','List the assumptions before estimating.']],[[
 '作者为什么先询问“实时”的含义？',['不同理解会影响设计','因为不打算做','因为所有页面都必须每秒更新'],0,'第一段解释了逐事件展示与定时摘要会引出不同设计。'],
 ['保留旧值的风险是什么？',['一定使页面崩溃','用户可能误以为它们仍是当前值','所有旧值都必然错误'],1,'风险在于误判数据时效性，而非一概认为旧值错误。'],
 ['目前记录下来的假设是什么状态？',['已经获批','已经实施','仍需确认，不能当作已批准要求'],2,'最后一段明确区分 assumptions 与 approved requirements。']
 ],{task:'用英文回复“让导出功能更快”这一模糊需求，提出需要确认的问题。',audience:'提出需求的同事',length:'100～160 词',requirements:['询问当前与期望耗时、数据规模','询问优先保留哪些行为或格式','说明确认前只是记录假设，不作过度承诺'],starter:'Before I start, could you clarify…?\nOnce we confirm…, I can…',model:'Thanks for the request to improve export speed. Before I start, could you share the current export time and the time users would consider acceptable? I also need the typical number of records and the largest expected export. Should the existing file format and column order remain unchanged? If an export takes longer than expected, would a progress indicator help users continue their work? Once we confirm these points, I can investigate the bottleneck and propose an approach. For now, I am treating the data size and target time as assumptions, not approved requirements. Please correct these assumptions before I estimate the implementation work.'});
